  "knowledge": {
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETE: shipped structure theorem (units mod 2^k) = <-1> x <5> (verified/0-ax), pivoting off the duplicate literal-value OQ.",
    "builtItems": [
      "EulerTotientOQ01OQ02OQ03.lean: 11 thm/2 def/166L, verified 0-axiom (only propext/Classical.choice/Quot.sound; decide is kernel not native_decide)",
      "isComplement'_neg_one_five (structure theorem), neg_one_notMem_zpowers_five (crux), disjoint_neg_one_five, orderOf_neg_one, orderOf_five (unit form), carmichael_two_pow (recovery)"
    ],
    "insights": [
      "Mathlib already proves the literal target lambda(2^k)=2^(k-2) (carmichael_two_pow_of_ne_two) AND parent EulerTotientOQ01OQ02.lean re-exports it, so the stated OQ is a duplicate; pivoted to the genuinely-new STRUCTURE theorem that explains the value.",
      "Crux not in Mathlib: -1 is not a power of 5 mod 2^k (k>=3), proved by reduction mod 4 (5=1, -1=3 mod 4). This is THE obstruction to cyclicity.",
      "Unit group mod 2^k is the internal direct product of <-1> and <5> via isComplement'_of_card_mul_and_disjoint (orders 2*2^(k-2)=2^(k-1)=phi, plus disjoint)."
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "Mathlib has ZMod.orderOf_five and abstract non-cyclicity but NOT the explicit 2-generator product decomposition of the 2-power unit group."
    ],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Bundle IsComplement' into an explicit MulEquiv to Multiplicative(ZMod 2) x Multiplicative(ZMod 2^(k-2)).",
      "Combine with odd-prime cyclic factors via CRT for the general structure of (ZMod n) units."
    ]
